			"notes": "First BedrockBridge release (**beta** — Windows is now verified working, please report any bugs you hit).\n\n## Platforms\n\n| Platform | Status |\n|---|---|\n| Linux x86_64 | Tested, works |\n| Linux aarch64 | Supported (untested on real hardware, but Playit publishes the daemon for it) |\n| Windows x86_64 | Tested, works (beta) |\n| macOS | Not supported (Playit doesn't publish official binaries) |\n\n## Installation\n\n1. Download \\`bedrockbridge-1.0.0.jar\\` below.\n2. Drop it into \\`~/.minecraft/mods/\\` (or your Fabric launcher's \\`mods/\\`).\n3. Make sure you also have Fabric API in \\`mods/\\`.\n4. Launch MC Java 1.26.1.2 with the Fabric profile.\n\nOn the first \"Open to LAN\" with \"Share with Bedrock\" ticked, it downloads Geyser/Floodgate/Playit (~25 MB, once) and prints a Playit claim link in chat. Accept the agent and the public endpoint for your Bedrock guest shows up in chat.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Minecraft Java **1.26.1.2** (alias 26.1.2)\n- Fabric Loader >= 0.19.2\n- Java 25\n- Fabric API\n\n## Localization\n\nChat / HUD / checkbox auto-detect your Minecraft language: any \\`es_*\\` locale gets Spanish strings, everything else defaults to English.\n\n## Notes\n\nThe .jar is cross-platform (it's Java code). The only thing that differs per platform is which Playit daemon binary gets downloaded at runtime. This release is marked **beta** because, while both Linux and Windows have been verified end-to-end, real-world usage may still surface edge cases — please open an issue if you hit anything."
		}
